+# Filtered Veterinarian Reads Bypass the Vet Cache
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+Both unfiltered read methods on the veterinarian repository are cached in a region named `vets`. That region is declared through the JCache API with statistics enabled and nothing else. No size limit and no eviction policy is configured, and the provider's own sizing mechanism is unused.
+
+`REQ-VET-003` adds reads narrowed by a specialty the caller names on the request. Spring's default key generator builds the cache key from the method arguments, so the caller's text would become part of the key.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Cache the filtered reads alongside the unfiltered ones.** Any caller mints one entry per distinct string, against a region with no bound.
+2. **Bound the region first, then cache the filtered reads.** Sizing the cache is an operational choice this requirement does not need, and vet cache invalidation is still an open question.
+3. **Leave the filtered reads uncached** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+The specialty-filtered read methods carry no caching annotation. The unfiltered methods keep theirs, so a request naming no specialty behaves exactly as before.
+
+No caller-supplied value enters a cache key while the `vets` region is unbounded.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A filtered request reaches the database every time. The clinic employs few veterinarians, so the repeated query is cheap.
+- The two read paths through one repository now differ in caching. A reader has to look at the method to know which applies.
+- Bounding the `vets` region stays open — see [Open Questions from the Survey](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey). Caching the filtered reads can be reconsidered once a bound exists.
+- The cache-key surface stays closed to request text. A later filtered read follows the same rule.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/vet/VetRepository.java` — the filtered and unfiltered read methods.
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/system/CacheConfiguration.java` — the unbounded region this decision works around.
+
+## References
+
+- [Veterinarian directory reads](../system-design.md#veterinarian-directory-reads) — the current state this decision produces.
+- [Filtering the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope](2026-08-12-non-goal-veterinarian-search.md) — the product decision that admits the filter.
