+### Veterinarian directory reads
+
+Both directory surfaces take an optional specialty on the query string. A blank value reads as an absent one, matching the owner search's treatment of blank input. A specialty no veterinarian holds yields an empty list rather than a rejection.
+
+Matching is on the whole specialty name. Case is folded in the query rather than in the column collation. The match is identical on all three vendors, unlike the owner search recorded under [Known Defects](#known-defects).
+
+Unfiltered reads are cached; filtered reads are not — see [ADR 2026-08-12](adr/2026-08-12-uncached-filtered-vet-reads.md). The HTML surface pages the narrowed list, and its paging links carry the specialty.
+
 ### Persistence
 
 The relational schema is not generated from the JPA mapping. `spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto` is set to `none`, and the schema is created by the per-vendor `schema.sql` scripts under `src/main/resources/db/`, with seed rows from the matching `data.sql`. The domain classes carry the JPA mapping annotations directly — there is no separate persistence model and no mapper between them. Under `architecture-principles.md` this is the sanctioned direct-mapping case: the project owns both the model and the schema, and the stored shape tracks the model closely.
